// The demo's model, for the REAL planner.
//
// This is what makes the demo an end-to-end test rather than a
// picture of one: legend-lite compiles the Pure that the snapshot
// serialiser emits, against this model, and returns SQL that
// DuckDB-WASM then runs in the browser. Same table, same columns,
// same types on both sides of the wire.
//
// `type: DuckDB` matters. legend-lite renders ANSI SQL through one
// renderer, but the connection type is what tells it which dialect
// it is speaking, and the browser plane is DuckDB.

###Relational
Database trades::DB
(
    Table TRADES
    (
        region VARCHAR(32),
        desk VARCHAR(32),
        book VARCHAR(32),
        year INTEGER,
        qtr VARCHAR(8),
        notional DOUBLE,
        pnl DOUBLE,
        qty INTEGER
    )
)

###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection trades::Conn
{
    type: DuckDB;
    specification: DuckDB { };
    auth: Test;
}

###Runtime
Runtime trades::RT
{
    mappings: [];
    connections:
    [
        trades::DB: [ c1: trades::Conn ]
    ];
}
